---
const retrievedNodes = [
  "RAG systems",
  "Web3 infrastructure",
  "GitHub repositories",
  "Relevant project records",
  "Proof links",
];

const ignoredNodes = [
  "Unrelated details",
  "Weak records",
  "Non-relevant coursework",
];

const outputNodes = [
  "Grounded fintech CV",
  "Role-specific application answer",
];
---

<section class="page-section vg-workflow-section" aria-labelledby="workflow-heading">
  <div class="vg-section-head vg-section-head--wide">
    <p class="eyebrow">Agent path example</p>
    <h2 id="workflow-heading">A task becomes a highlighted route through the graph.</h2>
    <p>
      For a fintech CV, the graph should not dump the entire career. It should highlight the relevant path, dim the weak
      path, and ground the output in selected records.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="vg-agent-path" aria-label="Example agent route through VitaeGraph">
    <div class="vg-agent-task">
      <span class="vg-route-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <p>Task</p>
      <h3>Create a CV for a fintech role</h3>
    </div>

    <div class="vg-agent-lane vg-agent-lane--relevant">
      <p>Relevant subgraph</p>
      <ol>
        {retrievedNodes.map((node) => <li>{node}</li>)}
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="vg-agent-lane vg-agent-lane--ignored">
      <p>Ignored path</p>
      <ol>
        {ignoredNodes.map((node) => <li>{node}</li>)}
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="vg-agent-output">
      <span class="vg-route-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <p>Output</p>
      <h3>{outputNodes.join(" + ")}</h3>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
